          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "GREAT GADDESDEN        POTTEN END HILL TL 00 NW                                         (North side) 5/120                                   Binghams Park -                                       II House. Early C17, altered to 2 cottages in C19, C20 additions to rear and sides. Timber frame older part, red brick newer parts, all plastered externally. C20 N part weatherboarded. Steep pitched roofs now slated. An irregular  1 1/2-storeys house oriented N-S with 2-cells,  internal- chimney, formerly lobby-entry house, and short gabled former kitchen wing projecting to E from S part of house.  2-storeys gabled later additions to SW and N, and lean-to entrance and stair extension E. Picturesque exterior with many gables, gabled dormers, large external chimneys, and casement windows. Round-headed oak entrance door. Interior has exposed timbers of wall-frame, clasped-purlin roof with straight wind-braces,  squint-butted scarf joint in wallplate, axial chamfered floor beams with bar-stop in main room N of chimney-stack, and scroll. stop in kitchen-wing. Some early C18 2-panel doors with H-hinges. Listing NGR: TL0306509577"
    }
